## G. General Terms

**G.1 Contributions.** Two kinds:

- **G.1a Repository contributions.** If you submit code, text, test cases, or other material into the Licensor's own repositories or releases, you grant the Licensor a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable license to use, modify, sublicense, and relicense it under any terms, and you confirm you have the right to grant it.
- **G.1b Enrichments.** If you record a Lineage Node under Section E instead, you keep ownership of your portion and your terms under E.5 govern it, subject to E.4, E.8, and P.6.

**G.2 Fix it and you keep it.** If you are notified of a violation, your license continues if you fix it and pay any amount owed within {{CURE_DAYS}} days. Otherwise it ends.

**G.3 Termination.** If your license ends, you must stop the use that needed it, and any amounts owed remain due. Late payments accrue interest at {{LATE_INTEREST_PCT_MONTH}}% per month or the highest rate the law allows, whichever is lower, plus reasonable costs of collection. Rights already granted under CC BY 4.0 for specification text are not affected.

**G.4 Names and marks.** This license grants no rights to the Licensor's names, logos, or trademarks, including {{MARKS}}, and {{SPEC_NUMBER_PREFIX}} numbers, except:

- you may state accurately that a work implements or cites a named specification; and
- you may say a product is "[Mark] Conformant" only while you hold a license under the applicable parts and the product meets that specification's conformance section.

A modified Specification text must not carry a {{SPEC_NUMBER_PREFIX}} number or present itself as the Specification.

**G.5 Definitions.** **Software** means the code, compiled code, schemas, test suites, test vectors, tools, and documentation the Licensor releases as part of a Covered Work, and later versions of them. **Derivative Work** means a work based on or derived from the Software: modifications, forks, translations, ports, rewrites in another language, and models trained or tuned on it. Using the Software's outputs, results, and reports is not a Derivative Work, and a component that connects at a declared Integration Point without copying, modifying, or linking in Software code is not one. An independent implementation written from a Specification alone is not a Derivative Work of the Software; Part P governs it. **Affiliates** means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with you; **Control** means owning most of an entity's equity or the power to direct its management. **Covered Work** means anything the Licensor releases under this license. **Gross Revenue** means all amounts invoiced or received, before any deduction; revenue from a bundle is allocated to each component at its list price. **Integration Point** means an interface a Specification declares for connecting third-party components. **Specification** means a document the Licensor publishes as part of {{PROGRAM_NAME}}. **Unit of Proof** means the measured outcome of one adversarial technique run against a target, as defined in the applicable Specification.

**G.6 Versions.** Each release is governed by the version of this license it shipped under. The Licensor may publish new versions, and you may choose to use a release under a later version, except that Section I carries forward unchanged into every version (I.2).

**G.7 Notices.** Anyone who receives a Covered Work from you must also receive this license, the Required Notice, and the Inventor Line.

**G.8 Assignment.** The Licensor may assign this license, its rights, and fees owed under it to any affiliate or successor. You may not sublicense or transfer your license.

**G.9 No warranty.** As far as the law allows, every Covered Work is provided as is, and the Licensor is not liable for any damages arising from it.

**G.10 Governing law.** {{GOVERNING_LAW}} law governs this license, without regard to conflict-of-law rules. Disputes belong exclusively in {{VENUE}}, and you consent to their jurisdiction.

**G.11 Severability.** If any part of this license is unenforceable, it is enforced to the maximum extent allowed and the rest remains in effect.

